"source": [
"# 00_sources · Brief A · Group 09\n\n",
"What this notebook produces: Data inventory, raw folder verification, and raw manifest verification.\n\n",
"What it needs: All files in data/raw/.\n\n",
"Owner: Group 09. Approach-log rows: 1-2.\n\n",
"Every section follows the same five cells: MAP (where this sits and what this section adds), DO (one idea per code cell), SEE (print the output), CHECK (an assert that prints pass or fail without stopping the class), SUM (what we now know, with its denominator)."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## CONFIG\n\n",
"Everything instance-specific lives here, so the notebook can be re-run on another half-year or another city by changing one cell."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"CONFIG = {\n",
"    'brief': 'A',\n",
"    'group': '09',\n",
"    'raw_dir': '../data/raw',\n",
"    'clean_dir': '../data/clean',\n",
"    'period_this': ('2026-01-01', '2026-06-30'),\n",
"    'period_last': ('2025-01-01', '2025-06-30'),\n",
"    'seed': 20261019,\n",
"}\n\n",
"import pathlib\n",
"import pandas as pd\n",
"import numpy as np\n\n",
"np.random.seed(CONFIG['seed'])\n",
"pd.set_option('display.max_columns', 40)\n\n",
"def check(name, condition, detail=''):\n",
"    print(('PASS ' if condition else 'FAIL ') + name + ('  ' + str(detail) if detail != '' else ''))"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 1 · Raw File Inventory Verification\n\n",
"Locate all raw input files and confirm essential folders exist."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### MAP\n\n",
"Step 0 in pipeline (Sources). Scans raw directory structure for required inputs."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### DO\n\n",
"Walk the raw data folder and index file extensions and file sizes."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"raw_path = pathlib.Path(CONFIG['raw_dir'])\n",
"all_raw_files = [f for f in raw_path.rglob('*') if f.is_file()]\n",
"df_files = pd.DataFrame([{'path': str(f.relative_to(raw_path)), 'size_kb': round(f.stat().st_size / 1024, 2)} for f in all_raw_files])"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### SEE"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"print(f"Total raw files discovered: {len(df_files)}")\n",
"df_files.head(10)"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### CHECK"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"check('Raw data files exist', len(df_files) > 0, len(df_files))\n",
"check('Plan data present', any('plan' in p for p in df_files['path']), 'plan file search')"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"### SUM\n\n",
"Discovered all raw files across legacy, nova, collections, plan, and patient directories."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Break it on purpose\n\n",
"Demonstrates hardcoding absolute local paths that break when running inside Codespaces."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
